### DQI-003: Synthetic Bounding Box Masking Actual Platform Coordinates
- **Severity:** CRITICAL
- **Source Files:** `all_routes_stops.json`, `all_routes_stops.csv`
- **Affected Elements:** Columns `stationlat1`, `stationlong1`, `stationlat2`, `stationlong2`.
- **Description:** 100% of rows (12,909 / 12,909) follow the exact artificial arithmetic offsets:
  $$\text{stationlat1} = \text{center\_lat} + 0.05,\quad \text{stationlong1} = \text{center\_lon} - 0.05$$
  $$\text{stationlat2} = \text{center\_lat} - 0.05,\quad \text{stationlong2} = \text{center\_lon} + 0.05$$
- **Root Cause:** An upstream GIS extract generated an arbitrary 0.05-degree ($\approx 5.5\text{ km}$) bounding box around the center coordinate point.
- **Impact on AI Agent:** If the caller asks "Which side of the road is the stop on?" or requests nearby stop navigation, using these coordinates would place the stop 5 kilometers away in rural terrain or agricultural fields.
- **Mitigation:** Designate `center_lat` and `center_lon` as provisional stop coordinates. Store the four bounding columns in raw audit lineage tables (`stg_station_coordinates_audit`); do not expose them to the spatial routing engine.
- **Confirmation Required:** Yes (Confirm that physical directional GPS surveys will replace provisional coordinates).

